      "math_academy_id": "e-8600",
      "problem": "Given that $X \\sim \\textrm{Bernoulli}(0.55),$ compute $P(X = 1                                                                                                                                                                                           \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                  ).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Bernoulli}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14273447/assets/c0ea18000253f48139163443876beb17be9e3ffd6c72c997000332de67f647e2.svg)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Bernoulli}(0.55),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14273447/assets/fa9929db95cdc2bdc4f637c657416ea013a32d771d42fa1ac7dd14cb92391714.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X = 1) = f(1) = 0.55.\n$$",
